| colspan="2" {{Tribebox-pt|lagi|S48 bianca t.png|60px|Bianca Roses}}
| colspan="2" {{Tribebox-pt|vula|S48 justin t.png|60px|Justin Pioppi}}
| On Day 8, coming in first place at the Immunity challenge, Lagi chose [[Kamilla Karthigesu]] from Civa, [[Bianca Roses]] from their own tribe, and [[Justin Pioppi]] from Vula to go on a journey. Each person had to play an individual game of chance where they had to roll seven dice, each of which had a face with a skull, a face with a flame, and four blank faces. Kamilla, Bianca, and Justin would roll the dice until they had rolled either four flames or four skulls; if they got four flames first, they would win an Extra Vote, but if they got four skulls first, they would lose their vote at their next Tribal Council. Kamilla successfully rolled four flames and won an Extra Vote. But Bianca and Justin rolled four skulls, meaning they had lost their votes.
|-
| {{Ep|4808}}
| colspan="3" {{Tribebox-tr|2|niunai|S48 kamilla t.png|60px|Kamilla Karthigesu|S48 shauhin t.png|Shauhin Davari}}
| colspan="3" {{Tribebox-tr|2|niunai|S48 mitch t.png|60px|Mitch Guerra|S48 star t.png|Star Toomey}}
| On Day 15 after the Immunity Challenge, upon which the first four people (Kamilla Karthigesu, Mitch Guerra, [[Shauhin Davari]] and [[Star Toomey]]) who were eliminated in the challenge embarked on a journey. There, they faced off in a challenge to keep their votes. The four of them were presented with a chute containing grey balls and red balls; each of them would take turns taking either one or two balls from the chute and placing them in their own chute. The first person to take three red balls would lose their vote at that night's Tribal Council. Ultimately, Star was the first to receive three red balls, meaning she lost her vote.
|-
| {{Ep|4811}}
| colspan="6" {{Tribebox-pt|niunai|S48 eva t.png|60px|Eva Erickson}}
| On Day 20, the [[Niu Nai]] tribe was instructed to randomly draw for one member to attend a journey; [[Eva Erickson]] was selected. There, she was tasked with stacking rows of tiles in a circular pattern on a spinning table that she could only move with her feet whilst balancing on a balance beam in the allotted time; if she stacked less than four rows of tiles, she would lose her vote at the next Tribal Council. If she stacked between four and seven rows, nothing would happen. but if she stacked at least eight rows of tiles, she would receive the Knowledge Is Power Advantage. Seeing as Eva was the only person in the game to possess any advantages or Hidden Immunity Idols, she opted to only stack enough tiles to keep her vote.
|-
| rowspan="3"|{{S2|49}}
| {{Ep|4902}}
| colspan="2" {{Tribebox-pt|hina|S49 matt t.png|60px|Matt Williams}}
| colspan="2" {{Tribebox-pt|kele|S49 jake t.png|60px|Jake Latimer}}
| colspan="2" {{Tribebox-pt|uli|S49 jawan t.png|60px|Jawan Pitts}}
| On Day 4, with [[Matt Williams]] from [[Hina]], [[Jake Latimer]] from [[Kele]], and [[Jawan Pitts]] from [[Uli]] were selected to attend a journey. There the three of them competed against each other in a challenge for an advantage. The castaways had to throw coconuts into the other competitors nets, once a net had enough coconuts inside, it would drop and that person would be out of the challenge. Ultimately, Jawan was the winner of the challenge. Jawan was given the choice of either making one of Jake or Matt lose their vote at their next Tribal Council in exchange for an Extra Vote for himself, or he could give one of the other tribes a [[Challenge Advantage|Challenge Disadvantage]] at the next Immunity Challenge. Jawan chose to take the Challenge Disadvantage, which he would ultimately give to Hina.
|-
| {{Ep|4905}}
| colspan="3" {{Tribebox-pt|hina|S49 nate t.png|60px|Nate Moore}}
| colspan="3" {{Tribebox-pt|kele|S49 mc t.png|60px|MC Chukwujekwu}}
| On Day 9, [[Nate Moore]] from Hina was selected by rock draw, while [[MC Chukwujekwu]] from Kele volunteered. Both MC and Nate were tasked to work together carrying a large load of sandbags to a barrel before an hourglass empties. Under the pile of sandbags was a stipulation to find an advantage before time runs out. Before finishing the task, both looked for the advantage, but opted to simply finish the task without finding it to ensure both had their votes.
|-
| {{Ep|4911}}
| colspan="6" {{Tribebox-pt|lewatu|S49 steven t.png|60px|Steven Ramm}}
| On Day 20, the [[Lewatu]] tribe was instructed to send someone for a strenuous journey. [[Steven Ramm]] volunteered to go. There, he was tasked with finding six signs with numbers around an island to unlock a combination box to retrieve a club to smash open a pot hanging on a post in the middle of the ocean. However, if the tide gets too high, then the pot will rise to the top of the post, releasing it, dropping it into the ocean, leaving Steven without a vote. Steven successfully completed the task, earning a [[Vote Blocker]].
|-
| rowspan="3"|{{S2|50}}
| {{Ep|5001}}
| colspan="2" {{Tribebox-pt|cila|S50 savannah t.png|60px|Savannah Louie}}
| colspan="2" {{Tribebox-pt|kalo|S50 mike t.png|60px|Mike White}}
| colspan="2" {{Tribebox-pt|vatu|S50 colby t.png|60px|Colby Donaldson}}
| On Day 4, [[Savannah Louie]] from [[Cila]], [[Mike White]] from [[Kalo]], and [[Colby Donaldson]] from [[Vatu]] were selected to go on a journey. There they were informed only two people could participate, with the third returning to camp immediately. After a rock draw, Mike was selected to return to camp. Savannah and Colby proceeded to play a game where they would take turns stacking odd-shaped blocks onto a tilting base, with the first player to knock over the tower losing their vote and the winner retaining their vote. Colby lost the challenge and therefore lost his vote, returning to camp first. Before leaving herself, Savannah was informed she had won an advantage in the form of a [[Vote Blocker|vote blocker]].
|-
| {{Ep|5007}}
| colspan="6" {{Tribebox-pt|manulevu|S50 stephenie t.png|60px|Stephenie LaGrossa Kendrick}}
| On Day 14, the [[Manulevu]] tribe was instructed to send someone for a journey. They decided to randomly chose someone using their [[Shot in the Dark]] dice, with [[Stephenie LaGrossa Kendrick]] being selected. Stephenie was tasked with playing a game of [[When It Rains, It Pours]] against a pot filling with water. If Stephenie could last for at least one hour, she would win an advantage, otherwise she'd lose here vote. She outlasted the pot, earning a [[Vote Steal]].
|-
| {{Ep|5009}}
| colspan="6" {{Tribebox-pt|manulevu|S50 christian t.png|60px|Christian Hubicki}}
| After winning the Immunity Challenge on Day 18, [[Joe Hunter]] was tasked to send one person on a journey. He chose [[Christian Hubicki]]. There, he found the {{wp|Jimmy Fallon}} One in the Urn twist. If Christian finished a puzzle of the season's logo before a barge capsizes, he would have the ability to cast a vote ahead of [[Tribal Council]], and the ability to [[Extra Vote|bank his vote]] (or not) at the next Tribal Council. If he could not, he would receive a letter to be read back at camp. Christian was unable to complete the puzzle in time and was revealed that he would be force to vote against himself at the next Tribal Council.
|}

